From: Lukasz M <lukasz1992m+openwrt@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 22:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: schedule the non-AQL txq on the hw of its phy

mt76_tx_check_non_aql() schedules the txqs of the station again with
ieee80211_schedule_txq(dev->hw, ...), which always resolves to the
primary phy's ieee80211_hw. On a device with one ieee80211_hw per band
(mt7915/mt7916 DBDC) every hw owns its own active_txqs list and
active_txq_lock. The txq of a station on the second band then gets
linked into the list of the primary hw under its lock, while the
scheduler of the second hw works on the same node under another lock.
That corrupts the list ("list_add corruption" in
__ieee80211_schedule_txq(), called from mt76_txq_schedule()).

Use mt76_phy_hw() with the phy_idx of the wcid, as the power save paths
in __mt76_tx_complete_skb() and mt76_sta_ps_transition() already do.

Also fixed in MediaTek's softmac_mt76 (1c944e4a, cherry-picked there from
10a3a40e4c2c).

Signed-off-by: Lukasz M <lukasz1992m+openwrt@gmail.com>
---
--- a/tx.c
+++ b/tx.c
@@ -253,7 +253,8 @@
 		if (!sta->txq[i])
 			continue;
 
-		ieee80211_schedule_txq(dev->hw, sta->txq[i]);
+		ieee80211_schedule_txq(mt76_phy_hw(dev, wcid->phy_idx),
+				       sta->txq[i]);
 	}
 }
 
